.TH SLURMON 1 "2026-09-07" "slurmon 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
slurmon \- interactive TUI for monitoring SLURM jobs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slurmon
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B slurmon
is a terminal user interface for monitoring SLURM workloads.
It displays a live list of jobs (via
.BR squeue (1)),
a historical view (via
.BR sacct (1)),
per-job details, and the tail of each job's stdout and stderr logs.
Jobs can be cancelled from the UI with confirmation (via
.BR scancel (1)).
.PP
The list, columns, sort order, and pane visibility are configured through
a TOML file (see
.B FILES
below).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to a TOML configuration file. If omitted,
.B slurmon
looks for one in the default location.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-squeue\-args \ ARGS
Extra arguments appended verbatim to the underlying
.B squeue
invocation. Example:
.RS
.B \-\-squeue\-args="\-u $USER \-p gpu"
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-sacct\-args \ ARGS
Extra arguments appended to the underlying
.B sacct
invocation used for the history view.
.TP
.BI \-\-scancel\-args \ ARGS
Extra arguments prepended to the
.B scancel
invocation before the job id (e.g.
.BR \-\-signal=TERM ).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-refresh\-interval " " \fISECONDS\fR
Seconds between
.B squeue
refreshes (integer, minimum 1). Overrides
.B job_view.refresh_interval
from the config file.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.TP
.B j / k
Move the selection down / up.
.TP
.B gg
Jump to the first job.
.TP
.B G
Jump to the last job.
.TP
.B e
Toggle between the stdout and stderr log view.
.TP
.B c
Cancel the selected job or array range.
.TP
.B C
Cancel the parent job (array root).
.TP
.B /
Enter search mode (matches id, name, state, time).
.TP
.B t
Toggle between the live and history view.
.TP
.B s
Cycle the sort key (none, id, name, state, time).
.TP
.B S
Toggle the sort direction.
.TP
.B Esc
Clear the active search filter.
.TP
.B ?
Toggle the help dialog.
.TP
.B F1
Toggle the footer.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/slurmon/config.toml
Default configuration file location.
.TP
.I example_config.toml
Reference configuration shipped with the source tree.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR squeue (1),
.BR sacct (1),
.BR scancel (1),
.BR scontrol (1)
